WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.197
The parliamentary record.

00:00:02.147 --> 00:00:11.056
What Parliament said — and what Parliament chose to ignore — while seventy-six thousand, seven hundred and seven Canadians were killed under Medical Assistance in Dying.

00:00:11.056 --> 00:00:15.739
Bill C-14, 2016: the original framework.

00:00:15.739 --> 00:00:18.534
Reasonably foreseeable death required.

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:20.943
A ten-day reflection period.

00:00:20.943 --> 00:00:23.556
Two independent medical assessments.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.681
These were the safeguards.

00:00:25.681 --> 00:00:28.102
They were designed to be temporary.

00:00:28.102 --> 00:00:30.511
They were designed to be removed.

00:00:30.511 --> 00:00:34.307
Bill C-7, 2021: the expansion.

00:00:34.307 --> 00:00:37.215
The foreseeable death requirement — gone.

00:00:37.215 --> 00:00:42.420
Track 2 created — MAID for chronic conditions, disabilities, non-terminal illness.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:47.068
Seven hundred and thirty-two Track 2 recipients in 2023 alone.

00:00:47.068 --> 00:00:49.136
People who were not dying.

00:00:49.136 --> 00:00:50.965
Killed by the state.

00:00:50.965 --> 00:00:56.852
The United Nations Special Rapporteur on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities raised formal concerns.

00:00:56.852 --> 00:01:02.136
The UN Human Rights Committee flagged Canada in their 2023 Periodic Review.

00:01:02.136 --> 00:01:08.749
Parliament's response: Bill C-39, delaying the mental illness expansion to March 2027.

00:01:08.749 --> 00:01:10.545
Not cancelling it.

00:01:10.545 --> 00:01:12.090
Delaying it.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:19.443
The Parliamentary Budget Officer estimated one hundred and forty-nine point five million dollars in economic savings from MAID deaths.

00:01:19.443 --> 00:01:21.840
That is the government's own number.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.454
They calculated how much money they save by killing people.

00:01:25.454 --> 00:01:27.204
And they published it.

00:01:27.204 --> 00:01:31.897
Veterans were offered MAID during calls about wheelchair ramps and housing support.

00:01:31.897 --> 00:01:36.011
Canadian Forces members tracked as priority expansion targets.

00:01:36.011 --> 00:01:39.204
The parliamentary record documents all of this.

00:01:39.204 --> 00:01:41.136
Every committee hearing.

00:01:41.136 --> 00:01:42.659
Every vote.

00:01:42.659 --> 00:01:44.363
Every silence.

00:01:44.363 --> 00:01:47.738
Hansard remembers what Parliament wishes you would forget.
